The most promising initial experiment

I would begin with CultureConnect, a relatively inexpensive service organizing voluntary social events around shared interests.

For example, a city could host recurring events for people interested in running, entrepreneurship, cooking, literature, or live music.

The events would welcome people from all backgrounds rather than assigning attendees to racial groups.

The company could measure whether participants develop new friendships, return to subsequent events, and report stronger social connections.

This would test a foundational assumption before investing heavily in a dating platform: whether the company can create meaningful relationships across existing social networks.

